---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import AvailabilityForm from '../components/AvailabilityForm.astro';
import { AWARDS, YEARS } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="The Story | DEEJAY T-JR., 3x DMC Canadian Champion"
  description="How DEEJAY T-JR. became the only woman in DMC history to win three consecutive Canadian national championships, finished top nine at the DMC World Finals, and competed at all four majors."
  path="/about"
  schema={[
    breadcrumbNode([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'The story', path: '/about' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="section tight pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Three years. Three national titles. <em>One</em> woman had ever done it.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The record is unusual enough that people assume it is a typo. It is not. Here is how it
        happened, and why it matters for the room you are trying to fill.
      </p>
      <nav class="jump small" aria-label="Sections">
        <a href="#dmc">The DMC years</a>
        <a href="#bastids">Bastids BBQ and the Toronto scene</a>
        <a href="#biography">Full biography</a>
        <a href="#awards">Awards</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lead">
        <div class="lead-media">
          <Photo
            name="portrait-studio"
            widths={[400, 620, 900]}
            sizes="(max-width: 820px) 90vw, 32vw"
            class="aboutimg"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="prose lead-copy">
          <p class="opener">
            She started competing because nobody in the room looked like her.
          </p>
          <p>
            Turntablism in Canada, like turntablism everywhere, was a men’s sport by default rather
            than by rule. The DMC Canadian championship had run for decades. No woman had won it
            three years running. In 2022, 2023 and 2024, DEEJAY T-JR. did — and the record still
            reads as an outlier because it is one.
          </p>
          <p>
            What a championship actually measures is preparation under pressure. Six minutes,
            judged, with no room to recover from a mistake. It is a harder brief than a ballroom,
            which is precisely why the ballroom is straightforward when she gets there.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="section panel" id="dmc">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>The DMC years</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The DMC World DJ Championships have run since 1985 and are the oldest and most demanding
          competition in turntablism. National champions qualify for the world final; the routines
          are six minutes long, performed live, and judged on technical execution, originality,
          musicality and composition.
        </p>
        <p>
          She reached the Canadian final for the first time after years on the Toronto circuit. In
          2022 she won it. In 2023 she won it again and carried the title to London, where she
          finished in the top nine at the Technics DMC World Finals — the strongest field the sport
          assembles. In 2024 she won the Canadian title for a third consecutive year.
        </p>
        <p>
          No woman in the history of the championship had taken three national titles in a row. The
          same year she was competing at DMC, she reached the technical category finals of the IDA
          World DJ Championships, which made her the only woman to have competed at all four
          majors: DMC World, IDA World, the Goldie Awards and Red Bull 3Style.
        </p>
        <a class="readmore" href="https://www.thehypemagazine.com/2026/09/17/who-is-deejay-t-jr-the-scarborough-turntablist-who-built-a-resume-that-couldnt-be-touched/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
          <span class="small muted rm-outlet">Read the full feature · The Hype Magazine · September 17, 2026</span>
          <span class="rm-title">Who Is DEEJAY T-JR.? The Scarborough Turntablist Who Built a Resume That Couldn’t Be Touched</span>
          <span class="small muted rm-by">By Jameelah “Just Jay” Wilkerson</span>
          <span class="tlink">Read it on The Hype Magazine <span class="arw" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="section" id="bastids">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Bastids BBQ and the Toronto scene</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Championships are won alone in a room with two turntables. Careers are built in front of
          people. Toronto’s scene — the crews, the barbecues, the annual gatherings where the city’s
          DJs actually play for each other rather than for a promoter — is where she learned to read
          a crowd rather than a judging sheet.
        </p>
        <p>
          That difference is the whole argument for booking her. A technically flawless DJ who
          cannot read a room is a liability at a wedding. She spent years doing both.
        </p>
        <a class="readmore" href="https://thesource.com/2026/09/18/good-music-good-food-good-people-deejay-t-jr-on-bastids-bbq-and-the-culture-behind-it/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
          <span class="small muted rm-outlet">Read the full feature · The Source · September 18, 2026</span>
          <span class="rm-title">Good Music, Good Food, Good People: DEEJAY T-JR. on Bastid’s BBQ and the Culture Behind It</span>
          <span class="small muted rm-by">By Shawn Grant</span>
          <span class="tlink">Read it on The Source <span class="arw" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="section panel" id="biography">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Full biography</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          DEEJAY T-JR. is a Toronto-based turntablist and the most decorated Canadian DJ of her
          generation. Between 2022 and 2024 she won the DMC Canadian DJ Championship three years
          running, and in 2023 she represented Canada at the Technics DMC World Finals in London,
          finishing in the top nine.
        </p>
        <p>
          Her competitive record spans all four of the sport’s majors. Alongside the DMC titles she
          reached the technical category finals of the IDA World DJ Championships in 2023, competed at the Goldie Awards in 2019, and placed third at Red Bull 3Style Canada in 2018.
        </p>
        <p>
          Competition is the credential; the work is the room. She performs for corporate clients
          including MLSE, the Government of Ontario and the Fairmont Royal York, for private events
          where discretion is the brief, and for clubs and festivals across North America, South
          America, Europe and Africa. Her audience is concentrated in the United States, Brazil,
          France, the United Kingdom and South Africa — current figures are in the
          <a href="/media-kit">media kit</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          She has showcased at NAMM and performed in Pioneer DJ product showcases. Through the GIE
          DJ Academy she teaches the next set of DJs coming out of Toronto, with particular
          attention to the ones who, like her, do not see themselves in the booth yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since then she has crossed to the other side of the table. In 2025 she hosted the 40th
          Technics DMC World DJ Championships in Tokyo, the first world final held in Asia, and as
          DMC Canada branch manager she ran the 2026 Canadian championships in Toronto. That same
          year she was invited to DJ Jazzy Jeff’s PLAYLIST Retreat. <a href="/latest">More on all three</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="section tight tan" id="awards">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Awards and results</h2>
      <div class="cols">
        <ol class="awards">
          {
          AWARDS.map((a) => (
            <li>
              <span class="atitle">{a.title}</span>
              {a.source && (
                <a class="asource" href={a.source} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                  {a.sourceLabel ?? 'Source'}
                </a>
              )}
            </li>
          ))
        }
        </ol>
        <ol class="years">
          {
            YEARS.map((y) => (
              <li>
                <b>{y.year}</b>
                <span class="small muted">{y.note}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </div>
          <div class="results-graphics">
        <h3>The results, as DMC Canada published them</h3>
        <div class="rg" data-reveal-group>
          <Photo name="proof-2024" widths={[320, 520, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 90vw, 28vw" />
          <Photo name="proof-2023" widths={[320, 520, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 90vw, 28vw" />
          <Photo name="proof-2022" widths={[320, 520, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 90vw, 28vw" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AvailabilityForm
    heading="Book her."
    lede="Send the date and the room. We reply within one business day with availability and a quote."
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .readmore {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 30px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--panel);
    transition: background var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .readmore:hover { border-color: var(--tan); background: var(--panel-hover); }
  .rm-title { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 25px); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--bone); }
  .readmore .tlink { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 4px; }
  .readmore:hover .tlink { color: var(--tan-lift); border-color: var(--tan); }

  .results-graphics { margin-top: 44px; }
  .results-graphics h3 { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--on-tan-soft, var(--muted)); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .rg { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; max-width: 900px; }
  .rg :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .rg { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .pagehead h1 { margin-bottom: 22px; max-width: 16em; }
  .jump { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 26px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .jump a { color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding-bottom: 3px; transition: color var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out); }
  .jump a:hover { color: var(--tan); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tan) 35%, transparent); }

  .lead { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 64px); align-items: start; }
  .lead-media :global(.aboutimg) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .opener {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.3vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.28;
    color: var(--bone);
    max-width: 20em;
  }

  .narrow { max-width: 900px; }
  article h2 { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .pending { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tan) 35%, transparent); font-style: italic; }

  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px); }
  .awards { list-style: none; }
  .awards li {
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  .awards li:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); color: var(--bone); }
  .awards li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 6px 24px;
  }
  .atitle { flex: 1 1 auto; }
  /* A result a promoter can click and confirm is worth more than one they have
     to take on trust. */
  .asource {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: color var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out), border-color var(--t-hover) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .asource:hover { color: var(--tan); border-bottom-color: var(--tan); }


  .years { list-style: none; }
  .years li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .years li:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .years b { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; color: var(--tan); }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .lead { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .lead-media { max-width: 380px; }
    .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
